      "topic": "The Four Basic Animal Tissues",
      "narration": "You feel the outer skin sheet, the firm muscle below, and a pinch sensation that reaches your brain instantly.",
      "ask": {
        "question": "Why do you think our body doesn't just use one single type of cell to do all these jobs?",
        "expect": "Different jobs require different structures, so cells specialise.",
        "hint": "Think about whether a cell that contracts like rubber can also transmit electrical signals or act as a waterproof barrier."
      },
      "show": [
